      "description": "Turns Windows' active internet check back on if a tweak tool turned it off. Without it Windows can show 'No internet' on a working connection and miss Wi-Fi sign-in pages, and apps that ask Windows whether you are online (Outlook, Teams, Windows Update and others) may act offline. A reliability repair, not a performance setting.",
      "risk": "systemConfiguration", "valueBasis": "documented", "activation": "reboot",
      "limitations": "On by default: on a PC nobody tweaked, nothing changes. A Group Policy that turns off the active tests overrides it.",
      "source": "Microsoft Learn 'NCSI troubleshooting guidance': default 1 on Windows 10 1607 and later; 'Don't disable active probing'; 'Make sure to set the value to 1'. The Registry Tweaks corpus sets it to 0. Added in the 2026-10-22 audit.",
