    {
      "id": "recommended-gaming", "name": "Recommended", "tier": "primary",
      "summary": "Everyday Windows with less promotion, ad profiling and nagging, and nothing you would miss.",
      "description": "Windows as you use it every day, minus what is there to sell or to ask for: no tips, suggestions, setup prompts or lock-screen and Start promotions, no advertising ID or tailored offers, no feedback prompts, no accessibility-shortcut prompts in the middle of a game, websites can't read your language list, and Windows sends only its required diagnostic data. Game Mode stays on and two Windows defaults are put back if a tweak tool changed them (the internet connectivity check and threaded DPCs; they change nothing on an untouched PC). Every setting is either documented by Microsoft or was checked on a Windows build, nothing here removes a feature you would use, and each setting can be undone from Activity. Optimisation is not the aim and no frame-rate gain is claimed. Windows keeps sending the data it requires for security, updates and reliability, and Edge, Microsoft 365 and other apps keep their own settings. The diagnostic-data policy needs Windows Pro or higher and administrator rights.",
      "operations": [ "input.accessibility-shortcuts-off", "notifications.no-feedback-prompts", "privacy.no-language-list", "repair.ncsi-active-probing", "repair.threaded-dpc",
                      "privacy.diagnostic-data-required", "privacy.no-advertising-id", "privacy.no-tailored-experiences", "notifications.no-tips-and-suggestions",
                      "notifications.no-setup-nags", "lockscreen.no-spotlight-ads", "start.no-recommendations", "start.no-account-notifications", "gaming.game-mode-on" ]
    },
    {
      "id": "maximum-performance", "name": "Maximum performance", "tier": "primary",
      "summary": "Recommended, plus fewer optional background functions and desktop power settings, with the trade-offs named.",
      "description": "Everything in Recommended, plus a more aggressive cut of what runs or reports in the background, and desktop power settings: Windows stops creating error reports, recording activity history, taking part in cross-device features, sharing updates with other PCs, tracking app launches, learning from your typing and showing Widgets; and on AC power the High performance plan, PCI Express links and drives stay at full power. Each addition is documented by Microsoft and can be undone from Activity. What you give up is named in each entry: no automatic crash reports, no Start 'most used apps' or Run history, no 'continue on another device', more idle power, heat and fan noise. No reputable measurement shows a frame-rate gain from these on current hardware; the aim is a PC that does less on its own, not a speed claim. On a laptop the plan and PCI Express entries don't apply (they would cost battery life), on a Modern Standby PC the plan doesn't (Windows offers only Balanced there), and on Windows Home the policy entries don't apply. Offered unticked: the unofficial telemetry controls (turning off the telemetry service and Windows' data-collection tasks, which Microsoft doesn't document as a way to reduce diagnostic data), online speech recognition, all app notifications, no USB selective suspend (Microsoft recommends leaving it on; for a device that misbehaves), hardware-accelerated GPU scheduling (a restart; needed for DLSS Frame Generation) and no NTFS last-access updates (a restart; can affect backup tools). Settings known only from community sources are never part of it.",
      "operations": [ "input.accessibility-shortcuts-off", "notifications.no-feedback-prompts", "privacy.no-language-list", "repair.ncsi-active-probing", "repair.threaded-dpc",
                      "privacy.diagnostic-data-required", "privacy.no-advertising-id", "privacy.no-tailored-experiences", "notifications.no-tips-and-suggestions",
                      "notifications.no-setup-nags", "lockscreen.no-spotlight-ads", "start.no-recommendations", "start.no-account-notifications", "gaming.game-mode-on",
                      "privacy.no-error-reporting", "privacy.no-activity-history", "privacy.no-cross-device-experiences", "privacy.no-app-launch-tracking",
                      "privacy.no-typing-personalization", "updates.no-p2p-delivery", "taskbar.widgets-policy-off",
                      "power.high-performance", "power.pcie-aspm-off", "power.disk-never-off" ],
      "optional": [ "services.telemetry-off", "tasks.telemetry-off", "privacy.no-online-speech", "notifications.off", "power.usb-keep-awake", "gpu.hardware-scheduling-on", "system.ntfs-last-access-off" ]
    },
